["Galois Theory and the Hilbert Irreducibility Theorem"],"prefix":"10.31979","author":[{"given":"Damien","family":"Adams","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"San Jose State University"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"16862","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/scholarworks.sjsu.edu\/cgi\/viewcontent.cgi?article=7803&amp;context=etd_theses&amp;unstamped=1","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2019,5,3]],"date-time":"2019-05-03T16:37:49Z","timestamp":1556901469000},"score":17.076649,"degree":["Master of Science (MS)"],"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/scholarworks.sjsu.edu\/etd_theses\/4256"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.31979\/etd.y7e3-xbdv"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,8,3]],"date-time":"2022-08-03T04:48:12Z","timestamp":1659502092392},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Oxford University Press","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2018,10,18]]},"abstract":"<p>Hale (2013) constructs and defends a conception of absolute modality as metaphysically fundamental. Part of this defense is an attack on alternative positions. One such position is a kind of modal skepticism that permits our declining to accept that any proposition is absolutely necessary. Another such position is a kind of modal reductionism that attempts to secure (non-trivial) modal truths via analysis that does not terminate in modal primitives of any kind. This chapter resists Hale on both fronts, arguing that the significance of the anti-skepticism established is variously limited and that the charge of question-begging against the reductionist(s) is not proven.<\/p>","DOI":"10.1093\/oso\/9780198792161.003.0002","type":"book","created":{"date-parts":[[2018,10,17]],"date-time":"2018-10-17T06:47:55Z","timestamp":1539758875000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["On Some Arguments for the Necessity and Irreducibility of Necessity"],"prefix":"10.1093","author":[{"given":"John","family":"Divers","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"286","container-title":["Oxford Scholarship Online"],"original-title":["On Some Arguments for the Necessity and Irreducibility of Necessity"],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2022,8,2]],"date-time":"2022-08-02T23:20:35Z","timestamp":1659482435000},"score":16.915184,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/academic.oup.com\/book\/7729\/chapter\/152829708"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2018,10,18]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1093\/oso\/9780198792161.003.0002","published":{"date-parts":[[2018,10,18]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,10]],"date-time":"2026-03-10T20:53:40Z","timestamp":1773176020048,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Institute of Mathematics, Czech Academy of Sciences","issue":"2","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Czech. Math. J."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1996]]},"DOI":"10.21136\/cmj.1996.127291","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,8,8]],"date-time":"2020-08-08T01:13:35Z","timestamp":1596849215000},"page":"291-308","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":13,"title":["Retract irreducibility of connected monounary algebras. I"],"prefix":"10.21136","volume":"46","author":[{"given":"Danica","family":"Jakub\u00edkov\u00e1-Studenovsk\u00e1","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"8849","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2008]]},"container-title":["Czechoslovak Mathematical Journal"],"original-title":["Retract irreducibility of connected monounary algebras. I"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/dml.cz\/bitstream\/handle\/10338.dmlcz\/127291\/CzechMathJ_46-1996-2_9.pdf","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2020,8,8]],"date-time":"2020-08-08T01:13:36Z","timestamp":1596849216000},"score":16.90118,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/dml.cz\/handle\/10338.dmlcz\/127291"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[1996]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"2","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2008]]},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1996]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.21136\/cmj.1996.127291","ISSN":["0011-4642","1572-9141"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0011-4642","type":"print"},{"value":"1572-9141","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[1996]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,28]],"date-time":"2025-11-28T10:06:56Z","timestamp":1764324416931,"version":"3.46.0"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,28]]},"group-title":"PsyArXiv","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Center for Open Science","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,28]],"date-time":"2025-11-28T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1764288000000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/legalcode"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<p>The debate over free will has traditionally been framed as a choice between libertarian indeterminism and hard determinism, with compatibilism attempting to reconcile freedom with deterministic causation. However, this framing overlooks a crucial insight from computational theory: that determinism does not entail predictability. We propose that the phenomenological experience of free will \u2014 the felt sense of open alternatives and genuine deliberation \u2014 corresponds to a real feature of complex systems: computational irreducibility. Drawing on Wolfram's taxonomy of computational complexity, we argue that human decision-making exhibits Class 4 computational behavior, meaning that outcomes cannot be determined without step-by-step simulation. This creates an epistemic gap between determinism (metaphysical closure) and predictability (epistemic openness) that grounds the phenomenology of agency. We defend this position against four major objections, including concerns about Libet's neurophysiological experiments, and conclude by proposing testable hypotheses for neuroscience and implications for artificial intelligence, moral responsibility, and the philosophy of mind.<\/p>","DOI":"10.31234\/osf.io\/e5ajp_v1","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,28]],"date-time":"2025-11-28T10:04:30Z","timestamp":1764324270000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["COMPUTATIONAL IRREDUCIBILITY AND THE PHENOMENOLOGY OF  FREE WILL"],"prefix":"10.31234","author":[{"given":"Rafael","family":"Reis","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"15934","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,28]],"date-time":"2025-11-28T10:04:31Z","timestamp":1764324271000},"score":16.73011,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/osf.io\/e5ajp_v1"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,28]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.31234\/osf.io\/e5ajp_v1","published":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,28]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,4]],"date-time":"2022-04-04T12:13:10Z","timestamp":1649074390526},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Institute of Mathematics, Czech Academy of Sciences","issue":"1","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Czech. Math. J."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1982]]},"DOI":"10.21136\/cmj.1982.101789","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,8,7]],"date-time":"2020-08-07T19:48:15Z","timestamp":1596829695000},"page":"116-121,122-128","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["On subdirect irreducibility and its variants"],"prefix":"10.21136","volume":"32","author":[{"given":"Ji\u0159\u00ed","family":"Vin\u00e1rek","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member